DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: drive a car with a differential and front steering.
# Model: Differential car. Motor A turns the back wheels through a differential;
# motor B turns the front wheels (it holds the left one's kingpin, a bar takes the right one along).
# The car drives ahead, goes once round a circle and backs up to where it started.
# Motor B steers by position, never further than 20 degrees: the steering stops near 30.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor stop action B hold
  set motor speed B 20
  run motor B to position 0
  set motor speed A 50
  reset yaw
  start motor A forward
  wait 2 seconds
  # Steer left and go round once: the yaw counts down to -180, jumps to 180 and comes back to 0.
  run motor B to position -20
  wait until (spike angle yaw) < -90
  wait until (spike angle yaw) > 90
  wait until (spike angle yaw) < 0
  run motor B to position 0
  stop motor A
  # Back up along the way it came.
  start motor A backward
  wait 2 seconds
  stop motor A
